<div class="start-card"><p><strong>Requires:</strong> prerequisite checks pass; subscription, region and source IP reviewed.</p></div>
<h2 id="cost">Cost check</h2>
<p>This creates paid resources. Allow roughly <strong>US$5–15</strong> for 3½ hours with prompt cleanup (11 November 2026 estimate, not a measured bill). VM, PostgreSQL, NAT and service tiers continue billing while the worker is idle. <a href="./reference.html#costs">Cost details</a>.</p>
<h2 id="stages">Start provisioning</h2>
{{snippet:commands.sh:provision}}
<ul><li><strong>01 → models:</strong> creates the tagged resource group and model deployments, then makes identity-based embedding/chat calls. AKS/database creation waits for this gate.</li><li><strong>02 → infrastructure:</strong> creates networking, ACR, Storage, queues, Key Vault, App Configuration, identities and telemetry; starts PostgreSQL and AKS/Functions deployments asynchronously.</li></ul>
<p>Defaults: <code>gpt-5-mini</code> + <code>text-embedding-3-small</code>, 1536 dimensions, PostgreSQL 17, one AKS node, Python 3.12 Functions Flex. Passwords go into Key Vault; never enable <code>set -x</code>.</p>
<details class="optional" id="network"><summary>Networking and infrastructure sources</summary>
<table><thead><tr><th>Traffic</th><th>Connection</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>AKS / Function → PostgreSQL</td><td>Private VNet + private DNS; no public database firewall rule</td></tr><tr><td>Workloads → Azure services</td><td>Public TLS endpoints, Entra identity, explicit NAT egress</td></tr><tr><td>Event Grid → Function</td><td>HTTPS Blob-extension webhook + system key</td></tr><tr><td>Browser → Products</td><td>Public HTTPS, source IPv4 /32 restriction and sign-in; private blobs</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Templates: {{file:infra/models.bicep}}, {{file:infra/foundation.bicep}}, {{file:infra/database.bicep}}, {{file:infra/compute.bicep}}. Separate delegated subnets provide Functions/DB integration. GlobalStandard model processing may occur outside the account region.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="while-waiting">Build while Azure runs</h2>
<p>Continue directly to Products. Stage 03 later checks readiness, with bounded waits and failed-operation diagnostics. Accepted deployments are not yet ready.</p>
<div class="verification"><strong>Verification:</strong> the model probe passes and the script reports AKS/Functions and PostgreSQL provisioning. These are expected results; <a href="./validation.html">observed validation</a> is recorded separately.</div>
<details class="optional"><summary>Troubleshooting</summary><ul><li><strong>Model probe fails:</strong> fix model access/quota/region before starting compute.</li><li><strong>ARM failure:</strong> inspect the reported operation for policy, SKU or regional restrictions.</li><li><strong>Name reserved/soft-deleted:</strong> recover your own resource or use a new prefix; do not adopt another group's resources.</li><li><strong>Interrupted:</strong> rerun the same stage/config. Scripts reuse matching resources and reject a group with another workshop tag.</li></ul></details>
